cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this book in your teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "Kiến trúc SOA & Microservices — Từ lý thuyết đến thực tiễn"
abstract: >
  A Vietnamese-language textbook on Service-Oriented Architecture and Microservices,
  designed for third- and fourth-year computer science students and practicing software
  engineers. Covers 12 chapters from SOA fundamentals and Domain-Driven Design through
  API design, distributed transactions (Saga), CQRS, Event Sourcing, API Gateway,
  security (JWT/OAuth2), observability, and production deployment (Docker/Kubernetes/CI-CD).
  All concepts are illustrated through a continuous case study: KBLab, a real-world LMS
  platform undergoing monolith-to-microservices migration. Accompanied by 102 interactive
  diagrams and a live pattern library.
